# Brusselator -- the textbook oscillating CRN.
#
#   A       -> X
#   2X + Y  -> 3X
#   B + X   -> Y + D
#   X       -> E
#
# A and B are chemostats and D, E are sinks, so all four are folded away: the
# first reaction becomes a zeroth-order influx and the third a decay of X into
# Y. What is left is the two-species core.
#
# The trimolecular step is the reason this network is here: it is the only one
# in the repo that puts two molecules of the same species on the left, so it
# exercises the k * n(n-1)/2 propensity branch that A + B -> ... never reaches.
#
# Rate constants are written for a system volume of 200 (concentration A = 1,
# B = 3). B > 1 + A^2 puts the fixed point at (200, 600) outside its stability
# region, so the system settles onto a limit cycle instead.

name brusselator
tend 40

init X=200 Y=400

0      -> X   ; k = 200
2X + Y -> 3X  ; k = 5e-5
X      -> Y   ; k = 3
X      -> 0   ; k = 1
